# 10. VERCEL-FRIENDLY TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

This requirement is mandatory.

First inspect the existing project's framework and preserve it where possible.

## Frontend

- Use the existing supported React/TypeScript setup if available.
- Build reusable components and clear page boundaries.
- Keep state management simple and predictable.
- Use a responsive layout.
- Optimize images and mascot assets.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Ensure every route works after refresh.
- Keep secrets out of client-side code.

## Backend and inference

If server-side AI inference is required, use a supported Vercel-compatible serverless route or the existing project's compatible backend.

The frontend must call a valid application endpoint rather than a Google AI Studio preview-only endpoint.

Use only the environment variables actually required by the chosen provider.

Validate all incoming requests and enforce reasonable input-size limits.

Check HTTP status codes and response content types before parsing JSON.

Handle:
- Missing environment variables.
- Invalid credentials.
- Rate limits.
- Provider outages.
- Network failures.
- Invalid JSON.
- Unexpected response formats.
- Timeouts.

Return consistent, sanitized error responses. Never expose API keys, stack traces, or internal secrets in browser errors.

Do not parse arbitrary HTML or plain-text error pages as JSON without checking the response.

Never claim that a production API route works until it has been tested.

## Free-tier constraints

Keep the architecture compatible with Vercel Hobby's current limits.

Avoid:
- Persistent background servers.
- Long-running processes that require a continuously running backend.
- Unnecessary database services.
- Expensive external APIs.
- Large mandatory downloads.
- Heavy client-side model inference that makes the site unusable.

Do not promise unlimited free AI inference. Explain any required provider configuration and current usage limitations.

If an open-weight model cannot be hosted reliably within the free deployment setup, use a compatible external inference service with transparent setup requirements or clearly labelled demo mode until inference is configured.

